==Enemy==
Does a serviceable amount of damage per hit, but her attacks are Single Target and she has next to no HP. More importantly though, she has a [[Barrier]] with a whopping 266,000 health!

==Strategy==
One UltraBaaBaa can be easily stalled using a couple of meatshields, but many of them at a time could be deadly under certain conditions, especially if they also come with other enemies. Her Barrier is basically her lifeline, so anything that gets through it will easily kill her. [[:Category:Barrier Breaker Cats|Barrier Breaker]]s like [[Fencer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Kendo Cat]] can typically finish the job, though any unit that can deal ≥266k damage in a '''''single hit''''' can also work.  [[Skirt Cat (Special Cat)|Loincloth Cat]] and [[Li'l Gross Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Macho Legs Cat]] are the most accessible [[:Category:Special Cats|Special]] options for Chapter 2 [[Aguham (Cats of the Cosmos)|Aguham]]. If you don't have a Barrier Breaker, then the [[Ototo Corps#Breakerblast|Breakerblast Cannon]] or a cat that can do at least 266k damage at once is needed or else you cannot defeat this stellar sheep.

Additionally, she can also be left unharmed on purpose so that Cats with [[Wave Attack]]s, [[Long Distance]], [[Surge Attack]]s or [[Explosion]]s can damage other enemies behind her first, like in [[Haunted Genome]] for example. Just remember to bring something else that can destroy her Barrier, or else the battle can't be won. She can also be used to stack up units such as [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] or [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] in stages where enemies spawn on base hit, if she appears as one of the first enemies.

